32: ERROR: mixed keyed/keyless sorts in the select block (L4) — `0.a^.b*` is a star branch whose landing and its sibling branches' do not agree: one level assembles a Map OR a tuple, never both. A star's landing follows its CONTENTS: Map contents splice in as KEYED fields, vector contents land as ONE KEYLESS component, and under `*` a key surviving before the star keeps the join nested under it. Here every branch is ordinal-headed, and under an ordinal head a star's landing passes through only when nothing between the ordinal and the star names a key; any other ordinal-headed branch is ONE keyless tuple component, whatever its `^`s. So make every branch a tuple component: keep a key before each star (`x{0.a.b* 1.a.b*}`, a tuple of records), or end the branch with `^` instead of its star (`x{0.a^.b^ 1.a^.b^}`). Selecting the flatten in its own block always works
33: ERROR: mixed keyed/keyless sorts in the select block (L4) — `0.a.b*-` is a star branch whose landing and its sibling branches' do not agree: one level assembles a Map OR a tuple, never both. A star's landing follows its CONTENTS: Map contents splice in as KEYED fields, vector contents land as ONE KEYLESS component; a total collapse (`*-`) always lands at its branch's top. Here every branch is ordinal-headed, and under an ordinal head a star's landing passes through only when nothing between the ordinal and the star names a key; any other ordinal-headed branch is ONE keyless tuple component, whatever its `^`s. So make every branch a tuple component: end each starred branch with `^` instead of its `*-` (`x{0.a.b^ 1.a.b^}`) — a total collapse keeps no key to nest under. Selecting the flatten in its own block always works
