37: ERROR: duplicate output key `:k` in the select block — two branches deliver the same output key, and distinct keys are required (strict merge; the alternative is a silent last-write-wins). The key may be one a branch NAMES, or one a star (`*-`) LIFTED out of its layer. Rename an UNSTARRED branch with `^k'` (`x{k^k2}`) — a starred segment cannot carry a rename — or select the flatten in its own block. Dropping the star of ONE ordinal-headed branch trades the collision for a keyed/keyless mix (L4): without its star that element lands as one keyless tuple component. Dropping it on every branch here gives a tuple of the elements. Through an ordinal, a star whose remainder names no key lands its fields at this level (Q_U61), so an element's lifted fields meet the level's other keys. `*-_` cannot tell elements apart either: an ordinal contributes no name to its prefix. To keep each element as its own tuple component, end EVERY branch here with `^` instead of its star (`x{0.a^.b^ 1.a^.b^}`).
