61: ERROR: duplicate output key `:port` in the select block — two branches deliver the same output key, and distinct keys are required (strict merge; the alternative is a silent last-write-wins). The key may be one a branch NAMES, or one a star (`*-`) LIFTED out of its layer. Rename an UNSTARRED branch with `^k'` (`x{k^k2}`) — a starred segment cannot carry a rename — or select the flatten in its own block. Dropping a star re-nests what it lifted — `*-` under its whole path — which resolves the collision unless another branch delivers that key too. Under a total collapse, `*-_` keeps each surviving ancestor's name in the lifted key (`x{a.k*-_ b.k*-_}` delivers `:a-k-…` beside `:b-k-…`), and an ancestor dissolved with `^` contributes no name — so drop the `^` where the branches differ.
